     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. The overdose risk is lactic acidosis, GI toxicity, and hypoglycemia when it's combined with other agents.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day total)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note recording that the dose was verified. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
